# VoiceVision Listen Mode
# Source: src/voicevision/listen.py

Listen mode entry point: voicevision-listen CLI

Features:
- Microphone → VAD → STT → text on stdout
- No LLM, no TTS - just speech in, text out
- Designed for editor keybinds (OpenCode dictation)
- Wake word mode: --wake-word "Olá Ambrósio" (default)
- Continuous mode: --continuous loops until Ctrl+C
- Pre-roll: --pre-roll-seconds N captures audio before wake word
- JSON output: --json gives structured transcript with metadata
- Quiet mode: --quiet / VOICEVISION_QUIET suppresses progress messages
- History: --no-history / VOICEVISION_HISTORY_ENABLED=0 opts out
- Custom hotwords: VOICEVISION_HOTWORDS points to JSON file with multiple words
- Multiple wake words: any match triggers (case/accent insensitive)

load_config() builds ListenConfig from environment variables.